  "title": "Building smarter communities through public-private collaboration",
  "summary": "LEaRN is a smart community initiatives that pairs Louisiana Consolidated Government with the University of Louisiana at Lafayette and CGI. LEaRN is working to deploy 300 low-cost air quality sensors as part of an Environmental Protection Agency (EPA) Smart City Air Challenge. It is also using this project to engage numerous community groups, including STEM education, civic engagement, healthcare and city planning stakeholders.",
